ry x="2244" y="2214" width="44" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="physical-c1141" value="PtP RF" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=8;fillColor=#FCE7F3;strokeColor=#DB2777;fontSize=9;fontColor=#0F172A;html=1;fontFamily=Inter;" vertex="1" parent="physical-L11"><mxGeometry x="2292" y="2214" width="44" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="physical-c1142" value="&lt;b&gt;Layers on this sheet&lt;/b&gt; (View ▸ Layers)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1 · Devices — Edit Data (Ctrl+M) = the &lt;b&gt;NetBox device record&lt;/b&gt; (name, role, device_type, rack, position, serial, primary_ip4, cf_*); grey pill = rack · U (links to the rack). Select a shape and click the link under it to open it in NetBox.&lt;br&gt;2 · Links — Po · speed · media · VLANs · port tags; Edit Data on a link = optics, cable ID, length, patch ports&lt;br&gt;3 · Mgmt IPs — &lt;i&gt;hide before sharing&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;3b · Serial numbers — toggle&lt;br&gt;4 · Circuit IDs — &lt;i&gt;hide before sharing&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;5 · Breakouts — cell notes&lt;br&gt;6 · Link register&lt;br&gt;7 · Asset register&lt;br&gt;Purdue levels, Border — &lt;i&gt;locked&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;Guides — &lt;i&gt;hidden&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Add a stack member:&lt;/b&gt; select a member row → Ctrl+D. It stacks and the box grows; then Edit Data for its serial.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Share with a vendor:&lt;/b&gt; run &lt;i&gt;netdiagrams share&lt;/i&gt; on this file (it strips IPs, serials, circuit IDs and the hidden data), or hide layers 3, 3b, 4 and 7 by hand, then File ▸ Export as PDF." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=20;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#E2E8F0;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;spacingRight=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontColor=#334155;fontFamily=Inter;" vertex="1" parent="physical-L11"><mxGeometry x="2370" y="1862" width="460" height="388" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="physical-L12" value="Border &amp; title block" style="locked=1;